   "title": "Start here",
   "widgets_values": [
    "# LongCat BF16 - Batch Audio (one video per voiceover) - 640 x 640\n\n640 x 640 (LongCat's 480p tier). Every 3.2 s chunk continues from the one before, with the portrait as identity reference on each window's last frame, pulling every chunk back toward the portrait pose. Every 40-60 s, in the middle of a real pause in the speech (mouth shut), the render starts again from the portrait itself: a full refresh against the noise that otherwise grows from chunk to chunk.\n\n**BF16 model** (31.7 GB): full precision, the reference quality. Needs an 80 GB GPU, or Block Swap below that.\n\n**Red nodes are the ones you set.** Everything else runs on its own. The stages run left to right, 1 to 7, each with a note underneath.\n\n1. **Load Portrait** - one person facing the camera, face clearly visible.\n2. **Audio From Folder** - put your voiceovers in `ComfyUI/input/batch_audio/` (.wav, .mp3, .flac, .m4a, .aac, .ogg, .opus). Each file becomes its own video, in name order. Upload them with Jupyter (port 8888) or FileBrowser.\n3. **Prompt** (optional) - leave empty, or describe the portrait in a sentence.\n4. Run with **batch count 1** to test the first chunk of the first file. Check `output/longcat_longform/<name>/chunk_0000.mp4`: lips, face, background.\n5. Run again with a large batch count: roughly the **total seconds of all files / 3.2**, plus a margin. Each run renders the next unfinished chunk of the next unfinished file. When every file is done the queue is cleared, so extra runs cost nothing.\n6. The final video lands in `output/`, then the queue is cleared.\n\n**Add files later:** drop them in the folder and run again; finished videos are skipped. The same portrait and prompt are used for every file.\n\nA 7-minute voiceover is about 130 chunks. If the batch count box stops at 100, click Run several times: the queue adds up.\n\nFull instructions: https://github.com/tenitsky/longcat-avatar"
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
