   "title": "About stage 1",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 1. Inputs\n\n**Portrait:** one person facing the camera, face clearly visible. The first frame of the video, and the identity reference for every later chunk. Any size; it is center-cropped to the canvas.\n\n**Canvas** (Width x Height), multiples of 16. LongCat has two tiers:\n\n| Tier | 1:1 | 16:9 | 9:16 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 480p | 640 x 640 | 832 x 480 | 480 x 832 |\n| 720p | 960 x 960 | 1280 x 768 | 768 x 1280 |\n\nLarger canvases need more memory and time."
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
  {
   "id": 4,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    1320,
    760
   ],
   "size": [
    520,
    420
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 3,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "title": "About stage 2",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 2. Prompt (optional)\n\n**Leave it empty** for a generic talking-head prompt: the person speaks to the camera, with small natural motion, a static camera and an unchanged background. The person and background themselves come from the portrait.\n\nTo steer it, type one or two sentences about the portrait, e.g. *A woman with brown hair in a navy blazer, in front of a plain grey wall.* They go in front of the generic prompt. Naming the background can help hold it in place on long videos.\n\nThere is no negative prompt: the distilled model runs at cfg 1, which does not use one. The text is encoded once and cached."
   ],
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000"
  },
  {
   "id": 5,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    1980,
